&CRN=INR
&RU=%22https://commerce.test.com/commerce/returntotest.jsp?payopt=ICI&redeemgc=n&gcertno=%22
&CG=Y


================================================================
6. CHANNEL RETURN URL (merchant-supplied "RU")
================================================================

The RU must:
- Be enclosed between %22 ... %22 (URL-encoded double quotes)
- Contain at least the merchant's mandatory query param (e.g. payopt=ICI)
- Be URL-encoded when placed inside ES
- Be encrypted as part of ES (NOT passed plain)

Example RU value (after URL-decoding the %22):
"https://commerce.test.com/commerce/returntotest.jsp?payopt=ICI&redeemgc=n&gcertno="

IMPORTANT: ICICI appends ES to this RU, so ensure the RU
           contains a '?' or is prepared to accept an appended ES param.


================================================================
7. RESPONSE URL (Callback - ICICI -> merchant)
================================================================

The bank calls the RU with ES appended.

SUCCESS callback:
https://commerce.test.com/commerce/returntotest.jsp
    ?payopt=ICI
    &redeemgc=n
    &gcertno=
    &ES=<ENCRYPTED_BLOB>

CANCELLED / FAILURE callback:
https://commerce.test.com/commerce/returntotest.jsp
    ?payopt=ICI
    &redeemgc=n
    &gcertno=
    &ES=<ENCRYPTED_BLOB>

The distinguishing field is INSIDE the encrypted ES:
- PAID=Y, BID=<10-digit>  -> success
- PAID=N, BID=0           -> cancelled/failed


================================================================
8. ES DECRYPTION - RESPONSE SAMPLES (decrypted)
================================================================

Success:
PRN=78945612396325871&ITC=1023814&AMT=1&CRN=INR&PAID=Y&BID=0125435380

Cancelled:
PRN=78945612396325871&ITC=1023814&AMT=1&CRN=INR&PAID=N&BID=0


================================================================
9. DOUBLE VERIFICATION (DV) - VERIFY URL
================================================================

Purpose:
- 1st check : decrypt ES from callback URL (done in return handler)
- 2nd check : call VERIFY URL using BID to confirm with bank
              (this is what the code calls "Double Verification / DV")

Method: GET
MD must be V (Verification)
NOT encrypted - all params sent plain in URL (per document)

Format:

https://payments.icici.bank.in/sm/BANKAWAY
    ?IWQRYTASKOBJNAME=bay_mc_login
    &BAY_BANKID=ICI
    &MD=V
    &PID=<PAYEE_ID>
    &PRN=<PRN>
    &ITC=<ITC>
    &AMT=<AMOUNT>
    &CRN=INR
    &BID=<BID>


DV / VERIFY URL PARAMETERS:

Parameter | Required | Description
----------|----------|--------------------------------------------
IWQRY...  | YES      | bay_mc_login (constant)
BAY_BANKID| YES      | ICI (constant)
MD        | YES      | V (verification mode)
PID       | YES      | Payee ID
PRN       | YES      | Payment reference number
ITC       | YES      | Item code (UPPERCASE)
AMT       | YES      | Amount with decimals
CRN       | YES      | INR
BID       | YES      | Bank payment ID from callback (10 digits)


DV / VERIFY URL RESPONSE:

Per document: HTML page
- Success   : "Your Payment is Successful"
- Not found : "Payment Record Not Found Check the Parameters sent"

NOTE:
- The document describes a simple HTML response for the verify URL.
- The current code (ICICIDvResponseDto) parses an encrypted JSON/key-value
  response with fields: atrn, prn, bId, paId, amount.
- This means your integration uses a NEWER encrypted-JSON DV API than
  the one documented here. Confirm with ICICI which API version is active
  in your environment (typically: newer encrypted DV endpoint).


================================================================
10. TRACKING URL (for TIME-OUT transactions - no BID available)
================================================================

Purpose:
- When a payment times out, the merchant has no BID.
- Tracking URL lets the merchant query by PRN + ITC + AMT + Pmt_Date
  (without BID) to find the BID and status.

Method: GET

Format:

http://payments.icici.bank.in/sm/BANKAWAY
    ?IWQRYTASKOBJNAME=bay_mc_login
    &BAY_BANKID=ICI
    &MD=V
    &PID=<PAYEE_ID>
    &PRN=<PRN>
    &ITC=<ITC>
    &AMT=<AMOUNT>
    &CRN=INR
    &Pmt_Date=<YYYY-MM-DD>


TRACKING URL PARAMETERS:

Parameter | Required | Description
----------|----------|--------------------------------------------
MD        | YES      | V
PID       | YES      | Payee ID
PRN       | YES      | Payment reference number
ITC       | YES      | Item code (UPPERCASE)
AMT       | YES      | Amount
CRN       | YES      | INR
Pmt_Date  | YES      | Payment date (format: YYYY-MM-DD)

Notes:
- ITC must be unique (this is how the txn is located without BID)
- Returns HTML page listing matching transactions with BID and status


================================================================
11. ENCRYPTION PROCESS - STEP BY STEP
================================================================

STEP 1 - Merchant builds ES plaintext:
    PRN=<...>&ITC=<...>&AMT=<...>&CRN=INR&RU=%22<...>%22&CG=Y

STEP 2 - Encrypt with EncryptDecryptUtil(masterKey):
    encDecUtil = new com.infosys.bankaway.icici.util.EncryptDecryptUtil(masterKey);
    String es = encDecUtil.encrypt(plaintextEs);

STEP 3 - POST/GET to ICICI with MD, PID, SPID (plain) + ES (encrypted).

STEP 4 - ICICI calls callback RU with ES=<encryptedResponse>.

STEP 5 - Merchant decrypts ES:
    String responseEs = encDecUtil.decrypt(request.getParameter("ES"));
    -> returns "PRN=...&ITC=...&AMT=...&CRN=INR&PAID=Y&BID=..."

STEP 6 - Parse responseEs. Check PAID==Y and BID!=0.

STEP 7 - (Optional) Call VERIFY URL with BID for 2nd confirmation (DV).


================================================================
12. FIELD-BY-FIELD CHEAT SHEET
================================================================

REQUEST (POST/GET):
    URL base : https://payments.icici.bank.in/sm/BANKAWAY
    Always   : IWQRYTASKOBJNAME=bay_mc_login&BAY_BANKID=ICI
    Plain    : MD=P, PID, SPID
    Encrypted: ES = (PRN & ITC & AMT & CRN & RU & CG)

RESPONSE (callback on RU):
    Encrypted: ES = (PRN & ITC & AMT & CRN & PAID & BID)

DV / VERIFY (GET, per document):
    URL      : same base
    Plain    : MD=V, PID, PRN, ITC, AMT, CRN, BID
    Returns  : HTML confirmation (legacy) OR encrypted JSON (newer)

TRACKING (GET, for timed-out txns):
    URL      : same base
    Plain    : MD=V, PID, PRN, ITC, AMT, CRN, Pmt_Date (YYYY-MM-DD)
    Returns  : HTML listing of matching txns + BID


