    bank_payment_id      VARCHAR(16),             -- BID / bId
    bank_atrn            VARCHAR(64),             -- ATRN
    bank_paid_flag       VARCHAR(8),              -- Y/N/0/etc.
    dv_status            VARCHAR(16),             -- SUCCESS / FAILED / NA

    -- Audit
    created_date         BIGINT,                  -- epoch millis
    created_by           VARCHAR(64),
    remarks              VARCHAR(512),

    INDEX idx_prn        (txn_ref_prn),
    INDEX idx_itc        (txn_ref_itc),
    INDEX idx_bid        (bank_payment_id),
    INDEX idx_atrn       (bank_atrn),
    INDEX idx_created    (created_date)
);


================================================================
6. INSERT FLOW - WHERE TO LOG EACH PAYLOAD
================================================================

Point 1: WEB_REQUEST
------------------------------------------------------------
In merchant's payment-initiation code (before sending to ICICI):
  - Build ES plaintext
  - Insert row: request_type='WEB_REQUEST',
                request_decrypted=<plaintext>,
                request_encrypted=<es after encrypt()>,
                request_url=<ICICI URL>, request_method='POST',
                txn_ref_prn=<PRN>, txn_ref_itc=<ITC>,
                txn_amount=<AMT>, txn_currency=<CRN>,
                merchant_id=<PID>, sub_merchant_id=<SPID>,
                created_date=System.currentTimeMillis()

Point 2: WEB_RESPONSE
------------------------------------------------------------
In ICICIRetailPaymentService.processICICICallBack():
  RIGHT AFTER decryption, BEFORE building DTO
  (line: "logger.info(...decryptedWebResponse)")

  Insert row: request_type='WEB_RESPONSE',
              response_encrypted=<raw ES from request param>,
              response_decrypted=<decryptedWebResponse>,
              response_url=<full callback URL>,
              response_method='GET',
              txn_ref_prn=<parsed PRN>,
              bank_payment_id=<parsed BID>,
              bank_paid_flag=<parsed PAID>,
              created_date=System.currentTimeMillis()

Point 3: VERI_REQUEST
------------------------------------------------------------
In ICICIRetailPaymentService.iciciDvinitiationProcess():
  RIGHT AFTER building DV request, BEFORE webClient call
  (line: "String dvRequestString = ...processICICIDoubleVerRequest1(...)")

  Insert row: request_type='VERI_REQUEST',
              request_decrypted=<dvRequestString>,
              request_url=<DV endpoint>, request_method='POST',
              txn_ref_prn=<PRN>, bank_payment_id=<BID>,
              created_date=System.currentTimeMillis()

Point 4: VERI_RESPONSE
------------------------------------------------------------
In ICICIRetailPaymentService.iciciDvinitiationProcess():
  RIGHT AFTER decrypting DV response, BEFORE parsing DTO
  (line: "URLDecoder.decode(...decryptedDVResponse...)")

  Insert row: request_type='VERI_RESPONSE',
              response_encrypted=<raw DV response>,
              response_decrypted=<decryptedDVResponse>,
              txn_ref_prn=<PRN>,
              bank_payment_id=<parsed bId>,
              bank_atrn=<parsed atrn>,
              bank_paid_flag=<parsed paId>,
              dv_status=<SUCCESS if paId=0 else FAILED>,
              created_date=System.currentTimeMillis()


================================================================
7. RETENTION & MASKING GUIDELINES
================================================================

SENSITIVE FIELDS
------------------------------------------------------------
- request_encrypted / response_encrypted
  -> Store as-is (encrypted = already safe), but consider
     column-level encryption at DB level.

- request_decrypted / response_decrypted
  -> Contains PII (amount, reference). Mask or restrict
     to audit role only.

- bank_payment_id (BID), bank_atrn
  -> Not PII by themselves but link to customer payment.
     Restrict to ops/audit roles.

RETENTION
------------------------------------------------------------
Minimum : 90 days (typical payment reconciliation window)
Recommended : 7 years (regulatory / audit)
Consider : Archive to cold storage after 1 year

ACCESS
------------------------------------------------------------
- Application role : INSERT + SELECT on PRN/BID for status lookup
- Ops role         : full SELECT
- Audit role       : full SELECT (read-only)
- Developer role   : NO access to *_decrypted in PROD


